WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.072
Homelessness crisis.

00:00:02.022 --> 00:00:04.431
The end of the housing pipeline.

00:00:04.431 --> 00:00:09.750
An estimated two hundred and thirty-five thousand Canadians experience homelessness each year.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.897
Encampments are visible in every major city.

00:00:12.897 --> 00:00:29.965
The crisis is the documented downstream effect of the housing financialization documented across this site: when housing costs eight times income, when vacancy rates approach zero in major cities, and when the system imports four hundred thousand people annually without building adequate housing — the most vulnerable are pushed onto the streets.

00:00:29.965 --> 00:00:33.318
And when they're on the streets, their health deteriorates.

00:00:33.318 --> 00:00:36.034
Mental health crises intensify.

00:00:36.034 --> 00:00:38.306
Substance use increases.

00:00:38.306 --> 00:00:40.454
Chronic conditions worsen.

00:00:40.454 --> 00:00:43.340
They become eligible for MAID Track 2.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.181
The housing pipeline ends on the street.

00:00:46.181 --> 00:00:48.602
The MAID pipeline begins there.

00:00:48.602 --> 00:00:51.124
The housing-to-homelessness pipeline.
